      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the computer repair process, begin by examining the hardware."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause establishes the process trigger (init) and prescribes the initial actions. The model faithfully decomposes this context into a start step and the examination step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the hardware has been checked, proceed with repairing any issues that were identified."
      ],
      "justification": "The unit directs moving to repairs after checking, referencing previously identified issues. The model captures this sequence by explicitly modeling identification and repair as consecutive steps, preserving the intended workflow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the necessary repairs have been made, conclude the hardware inspection."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct correspondence to the instruction to wrap up the inspection following the first round of repairs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following the completion of the repair process, it is important to test the functionality of the system."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match to the prescribed testing step after repairs."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "guard:b2->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the test results indicate that everything is functioning properly, then the hardware inspection process can be concluded."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional unit justifies the XOR branch, the success-path guard (abstracted as 'Yes'), the concluding action, and the implicit terminal node. The condition is correctly modeled as a decision action per acceptable practice."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n11",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the test results indicate that there are still issues, then further hardware repairs are required."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps the failure-condition guard (abstracted as 'No') and the mandated follow-up repair action for the negative branch."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once these additional repairs have been made, the hardware inspection process can be concluded."
      ],
      "justification": "Corresponds to the final closure step and implicit process termination after the second repair loop completes."
    }
  ],
